# FAQ page.

title "Frequently asked questions"

space

section
    title "What is EZHTML?"
    text "EZHTML is a modern, indentation-based markup language that compiles to clean HTML5."

section
    title "Why not just HTML?"
    text "HTML has 30 years of accumulated syntax. EZHTML keeps the parts you actually use and rebuilds the rest around indentation."

section
    title "Can I use my existing CSS?"
    text "Yes. Class names are stable: `.btn`, `.card`, `.row`, `.col`, `.container`, `.title`."

section
    title "What about JavaScript?"
    text "JavaScript is unchanged. You can drop in a `<script>` via the `html` pass-through element."
